  "lead_raw_text": " The structure of CaZr₂ crystallizes in the hexagonal space group P6₃/mmc (No. 194), with a unit cell containing six atoms—two Ca and four Zr—distributed over two independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis shows both Ca and Zr centers adopt a close-packed-like local arrangement with 12 geometric neighbors each; Ca is coordinated by 12 Zr neighbors, while Zr is surrounded by 4 Ca and 8 Zr neighbors. These 12-vertex coordination polyhedra connect into a single three-dimensional geometric neighbor graph spanning all six sites. Validated polyhedron-sharing analysis indicates that Zr–Zr 12-vertex polyhedra exhibit corner-, edge-, and face-sharing, and Ca–Zr pairs share edges.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
